    "cross_source_insight": "While human designers prioritize narrative understanding and spatial context to create emotionally resonant lighting and sets (01-c1, 01-c3), AI tools like AuraLuxMuse demonstrate the capability to assist by automating lighting cue generation aligned with music and aesthetics, offering speed but relying on structured data and designer input (01-c4, 01-c5).",
    "limitation": "The AI system evaluated is limited by its controlled experimental dataset (~150 minutes of paired cues), lacks large-scale benchmarks, and does not yet fully address personalization or complete lighting parameterization, indicating it cannot fully replace human creative judgment (01-c4). Also, designer interviews reflect individual perspectives, not universal practices."
